notes = "(!) Save states and netplay are not supported - Eden has no state serialization for this core.|(!) Renders headlessly and copies the finished frame back to the frontend rather than sharing a GPU context, so expect a performance cost versus standalone Eden.|(!) Requires Switch prod.keys - by default (eden_use_frontend_dirs core option) expected under system_directory/keys, alongside config, cache, shaders and logs.|(!) NAND, SDMC, saves, screenshots and other user data are placed directly under save_directory by default, so RetroArch's own save handling covers them.|(!) Disable the eden_use_frontend_dirs core option to use a standalone Eden install's existing %APPDATA%/Eden (or portable user/) data instead.|(!) This core is a community port of suyu's libretro core (itself a fork of Eden) - not an official Eden Project release."

description = "A port of the Eden Nintendo Switch emulator to libretro, adapted from suyu's own libretro core (suyu being a fork of Eden). Eden implements HLE emulation of the Switch's CPU, GPU and OS services. This core is an early/experimental port: it renders internally and reads the frame back for the frontend rather than sharing a hardware context, and does not yet support save states or netplay."
